{"id":"24fc855c-2294-4b7d-acab-d22ee0399b56","expr":"str != null","rationale":"Since the method returns immediately if str is null, it is meaningful to assume str is non-null for further logic.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOfIgnoreCaseAscii(CharSequence,CharSequence,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.386799169Z"}
{"id":"c4a23197-3323-4ef6-a55a-135e8d786d83","expr":"searchStr != null","rationale":"Similar to str, the method returns if searchStr is null, so it can be treated as non-null after the null check.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOfIgnoreCaseAscii(CharSequence,CharSequence,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.386799169Z"}
{"id":"d94a7aa2-2879-4038-ac7a-9320b60e1820","expr":"startPos >= 0","rationale":"Negative startPos values are normalized to 0, so startPos is effectively always >= 0 during main processing.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOfIgnoreCaseAscii(CharSequence,CharSequence,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.386799169Z"}
{"id":"ccc1e4ca-7b54-444b-9e8a-8e0083f30ac7","expr":"startPos <= str.length()","rationale":"startPos is bounded above by the last possible index where searchStr can match in str.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOfIgnoreCaseAscii(CharSequence,CharSequence,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.386799169Z"}
{"id":"1ad4d7c7-0646-42b1-8609-486b6ce52792","expr":"searchStr.length() <= str.length()","rationale":"searchStr length cannot exceed str length for indexOfIgnoreCaseAscii to find a match.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOfIgnoreCaseAscii(CharSequence,CharSequence,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.386799169Z"}
{"id":"63531b64-0210-4c8f-b818-830154f5f056","expr":"(b >= 0 && b <= 127)","rationale":"The input byte 'b' should represent an ASCII character, therefore it lies within the ASCII range 0-127.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toUpperCase(byte):byte","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.440926397Z"}
{"id":"6a216a87-3695-467c-92c7-69add606f428","expr":"((b >= 97 && b <= 122) || (b < 97 || b > 122))","rationale":"Byte 'b' can be either a lowercase ASCII letter (a-z) or not, preparing for toUpperCase conversion.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toUpperCase(byte):byte","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.440926397Z"}
{"id":"8c589ca4-b6b4-41cc-a20c-b0c1aff7c749","expr":"((b < 97) || (b > 122) || (b >= 97 && b <= 122))","rationale":"This expresses the byte 'b' is either not a lowercase letter or is a lowercase letter in ASCII.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toUpperCase(byte):byte","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.440926397Z"}
{"id":"3a6f4a5d-b5d9-4e32-8399-58364e5aff37","expr":"(b >= 0)","rationale":"The byte 'b' is non-negative to represent a valid ASCII character.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toUpperCase(byte):byte","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.440926397Z"}
{"id":"3deee022-814f-44e5-a457-5083a7e3a128","expr":"(b <= 127)","rationale":"The byte 'b' does not exceed the maximum ASCII value of 127.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toUpperCase(byte):byte","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.440926397Z"}
{"id":"802f1714-1a23-4216-92fd-35f12991d510","expr":"result >= 0 && result <= 127","rationale":"Since input and output are ASCII bytes, result must be a valid ASCII character.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toUpperCase(byte):byte","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:03.462189896Z"}
{"id":"744c39aa-9290-4cb0-8be3-05ae8e7af83e","expr":"result >= -1","rationale":"The method returns either -1 (INDEX_NOT_FOUND) or a valid index position.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOf(CharSequence,char,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:05.133101117Z"}
{"id":"a3931b50-082a-4864-b1d3-52da105e0e5b","expr":"result >= start || result == -1","rationale":"The search starts from start index; thus found index cannot be before start.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOf(CharSequence,char,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:05.133101117Z"}
{"id":"814bc1fb-4458-4bc1-9beb-5bc6021e4789","expr":"cs == null || (result == -1 || (result < cs.length()))","rationale":"Valid index is within the bounds of cs; if cs is null, result is -1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOf(CharSequence,char,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:05.133101117Z"}
{"id":"fe7a5c84-c7ba-42ff-9524-e49cde7cbc49","expr":"cs == null || (result == -1 || cs.charAt(result) == searchChar)","rationale":"The method returns the index where searchChar is found.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOf(CharSequence,char,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:05.133101117Z"}
{"id":"7dfacd79-0492-4200-8f34-c5ed3d0d67fa","expr":"start >= 0 || result == -1","rationale":"Negative start is adjusted internally to zero; thus results are consistent.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#indexOf(CharSequence,char,int):int","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:05.133101117Z"}
{"id":"30a5fdf2-1118-4283-a8c5-1e5c14bc0f97","expr":"value >= 0","rationale":"char values in Java are always non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#isUpperCase(char):boolean","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:05.257770423Z"}
{"id":"4dd916ae-83ad-400e-bc5e-e70f2a692617","expr":"Character.isUpperCase(c) || !Character.isUpperCase(c)","rationale":"c is a character that can be uppercase or not.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toLowerCase(char):char","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:06.325946304Z"}
{"id":"56337010-7fa6-4c87-ac60-8dc6995f52c1","expr":"c >= 0","rationale":"c is non-negative since char is unsigned.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toLowerCase(char):char","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:06.325946304Z"}
{"id":"612a2bd4-afe3-40cc-9746-1d35d23a6564","expr":"c <= Character.MAX_VALUE","rationale":"c lies within valid char range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toLowerCase(char):char","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:06.325946304Z"}
{"id":"0542ba20-ab0b-4e8b-a78d-7cae059b4e23","expr":"!result || (value >= 65 && value <= 90)","rationale":"Uppercase letters in ASCII have byte values from 65 ('A') to 90 ('Z'). The method returns true if and only if value is in this range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#isUpperCase(byte):boolean","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:06.636209965Z"}
{"id":"3d78d452-1fc2-4bf8-a25a-6f891180fbc4","expr":"result || (value < 65 || value > 90)","rationale":"Negation of the above invariant to cover the false case.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#isUpperCase(byte):boolean","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:06.636209965Z"}
{"id":"e634b7c4-2dd9-4fbd-8c43-71422bc43143","expr":"value >= 0","rationale":"ASCII values to check case should be non-negative as ASCII codes are in range 0-127.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#isUpperCase(byte):boolean","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:07.425632308Z"}
{"id":"2d8fb63c-23d2-4318-ab5b-48d71b9d6d38","expr":"value <= 127","rationale":"Uppercase letters are in ASCII range 65 ('A') to 90 ('Z'), which is within 0 to 127.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#isUpperCase(byte):boolean","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:07.425632308Z"}
{"id":"e256be41-b4ab-46b8-912e-5b30dafd04ab","expr":"(value >= 65 && value <= 90) == true || (value < 65 || value > 90)","rationale":"The input byte is only an uppercase ASCII letter if its code is between 65 and 90 inclusive.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#isUpperCase(byte):boolean","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:07.425632308Z"}
{"id":"bc72e592-53b8-4faf-8020-0dfdda90ac17","expr":"!(value >= 97 && value <= 122)","rationale":"If the value is uppercase, it cannot be a lowercase letter.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#isUpperCase(byte):boolean","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:07.425632308Z"}
{"id":"df872cd1-e0c4-4a30-ae7d-d720dadbf367","expr":"(value >= 65 && value <= 90) || (value < 65 || value > 90)","rationale":"The method checks if the character is an uppercase ASCII letter by comparing value within ASCII uppercase letter range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#isUpperCase(byte):boolean","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:07.425632308Z"}
{"id":"3d6fab21-698a-4f18-b257-ec49e0c1d8d3","expr":"Character.toLowerCase(c) == result","rationale":"The result should be the lowercase equivalent of c as per Character.toLowerCase.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toLowerCase(char):char","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:07.431540572Z"}
{"id":"f058cbe8-00ff-4b1d-8286-91599e789989","expr":"!(Character.isUpperCase(c) && result == c)","rationale":"If c is uppercase, result can't be unchanged.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#toLowerCase(char):char","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:07.431540572Z"}
{"id":"cefbde4e-e620-4f70-a506-374d118a78dd","expr":"b >= -128 && b <= 127","rationale":"b is a byte, which ranges from -128 to 127","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.AsciiString#b2c(byte):char","file":"io/netty/util/AsciiString.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T11:46:09.095166697Z"}
